Investigate an inlet, line and counter together (@cm-study-sampling-chain: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Aerosol-Instrument-Calibration-Chen-Fletcher-Cheng.lingua#r_03PDE8353KQ9HQKJNAHRH99NPP", #source "../sources/Mobility-Particle-Size-Spectrometers-Wiedensohler.lingua#r_1W06WPADV43B98EF8NSW9RDCWM", #clean-manufacturing "Review-what-the-aerosol-measurements-establish.lingua#r_29HS8QY95V57MXZ2W8TS62TDEZ") { r_09KGTHY49N9ZWR6Q39R41P3Z8W
**Read:** [Calibration of aerosol instruments — Chen, Fletcher and Cheng](../sources/Aerosol-Instrument-Calibration-Chen-Fletcher-Cheng.lingua#r_03PDE8353KQ9HQKJNAHRH99NPP), apparatus and flow; [Mobility particle size spectrometers — Wiedensohler and colleagues](../sources/Mobility-Particle-Size-Spectrometers-Wiedensohler.lingua#r_1W06WPADV43B98EF8NSW9RDCWM), loss corrections. Use [Define the observed population and the sampling boundary](../aerosol-measurement/Define-the-observed-population-and-the-sampling-boundary.lingua#r_1YX75Q8RYV60TB8ZPFD0TK10VC) through [Drying, diluting and heating can change the measurand](../aerosol-measurement/Drying-diluting-and-heating-can-change-the-measurand.lingua#r_4B2HNNY2K011H9VAN6M2E2QNA3).

Choose an airborne population with at least three size groups and a time-dependent release. Specify location, gas state, sampling geometry, flows, line segments and detector efficiencies. Forward-predict expected observations and compare them with the source population and with exposure at a sensitive surface.

Begin with independently checkable limits: no loss, perfect detection, constant concentration and instantaneous response. Add one mechanism at a time. Check particle-number accounting across splits and distinguish gas-volume normalization from physical growth or evaporation. Use the simple tube model only within its declared teaching assumptions.

Introduce one unknown loss or delayed release and ask whether the count history identifies it separately from a changed source. Propose a shortened-path, changed-flow or independent-position comparison, accounting for what else the change affects.

**Result to explain:** A reproducible observation model, predicted counts, uncertainty and a supported statement about the sampled population. Explain why that statement does or does not extend to the whole room, a transfer event or product deposition. Report the informative next observation when the available data leave competing explanations.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
**Continue in clean manufacturing:** [Review what the aerosol measurements establish](Review-what-the-aerosol-measurements-establish.lingua#r_29HS8QY95V57MXZ2W8TS62TDEZ).

